<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
The entitlements of C-0009 section 4 that the app declares itself. increased-memory-limit is
declared explicitly, because the .NET build does not copy it from the profile. get-task-allow
comes from the development profile when the user's sideloading tool re-signs the app, so it is
not here. extended-virtual-addressing is added only when the build property
PaneportExtendedVirtualAddressing is true: a signing build adds it through AppHead.props, and
eng/mac/sign-adhoc.sh adds it when PANEPORT_EXTENDED_VIRTUAL_ADDRESSING is true.
-->
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
